{
  "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
  "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "From 1790 to 1891, foreigners were categorically ineligible to hold U.S. copyrights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Omega, S.A.",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Omega says \"lawfully made under this title\" means either made in the United States or authorized for distribution in the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Would you clarify for me what your exact meaning is?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Motion Picture Association of America",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Motion Picture Association of America has filed an amicus brief in this case, and on page 19 of its brief, the MPAA says that the result the government says is A-OK is, quote, \"a nonsensical and unintended consequence.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My question really wasn't to argue with you. My question was: Where in the legislative history does it say that the point of 602 is to prevent a foreign publisher from selling copies to a distributor and then that distributor resells them to the United States?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Aaron M. Panner",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section -- section 602(a)(1) allows the distribution of foreign-made copies abroad without the U.S. copyright holder forfeiting the exclusive right to distribute copies domestically, which is guaranteed by section 106(3), and that provision applies in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Aaron M. Panner",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\"Made\" certainly includes the creation of the physical copy. It also includes the addition of any necessary intellectual property rights that would permit distribution in the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Aaron M. Panner",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 602(a)(1) is designed to permit a U.S. copyright owner to exclude legitimate copies, and if you ask where Congress said that, it's right in the House Committee report, in the legislative history."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the government's interpretation of section 109(a) is a little bit different from either of the parties, since I want to make clear precisely what it is, in our view, the words \"lawfully made under this title\" mean made subject to and in accordance with Title 17. And because the Copyright Act doesn't apply abroad, in order for a copy to be made subject to Title 17, it would have to be created in the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, what is your answer to the argument that if \"lawfully made under this title\" means basically made in the United States, that provides a great incentive to manufacture goods abroad and that can't possibly be what Congress intended?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, in your example, if there is a lawful importation of the foreign-made good, then if you interpret \"made\" as causing to exist of appear or under these laws, as the library brief suggests, the first sale doctrine would operate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why don't we let contract law control the violations of any agreements with foreigners?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roy T. Englert, Jr.",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF ROY T. ENGLERT, JR., ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER\n\nMR. ENGLERT: Thank you, Your Honor.\n\nJustice Ginsberg asked Mr. Panner what policy Congress could have had in mind to give this different status to foreign-made goods than to U.S. made goods, and Mr. Panner's answer, and Mr. Stewart said something similar, was that in one respect Congress is disfavoring foreign goods under their interpretation by making them harder to import. That's not true."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roy T. Englert, Jr.",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "81892cb75c4ad1a222d32c3df0f94f6a437f41f6e45a7d6371b931e981491b7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-81892cb75c4a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the briefs in this case you will not find anyone making any policy argument as to what Congress could have had in mind to favor foreign-manufactured goods."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-08-1423",
      "confidence": 0.0,
